<%# ============================================================================
    DATASETS — the public corpora this studio draws from.

    Two datasets, and the page states WHICH KIND of useful each one is, because
    they are not the same thing:

      * DiffusionDB gives PROMPTS. Real sentences with the hyperparameters their
        authors used and the dataset's own 2-D projection of prompt space, so
        this section BROWSE, SEARCHES, MAPS and GENERATES FROM them.
      * MET-Meme gives a SCHEMA. Its annotation vocabulary is what a meme
        artefact here is labelled with, and its IMAGES are deliberately absent —
        they live on Kaggle under the dataset's own terms, so the page says so
        rather than implying the pictures are here.

    Nothing on this page writes a job of its own: "Use on Run Job" carries a
    prompt to the form as a DEFAULT the operator then edits.
    ============================================================================ %>
<div class="page-head">
  <div class="page-head-row page-head-row--split page-head-row--stacked">
    <h1 class="section-title"><span class="gradient-text">Datasets</span></h1>
    <p class="page-head-blurb page-head-blurb--long">
      Public corpora this studio draws from, kept with their provenance. The
      prompt library is FED TO the generator — a prompt drawn here is generated
      for real — and the label vocabulary is what a meme artefact is annotated
      with. Neither dataset's own images are copied here:
      <%= link_to "DiffusionDB", "https://github.com/poloclub/diffusiondb" %> is
      CC0-1.0 prompts, and MET-Meme's images stay
      <%= link_to "on Kaggle", MemeVocabulary::SOURCE["images_url"] %> under its own
      terms.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="page-sub">
    <div class="page-sub-main">
      <div class="job-stat"><span class="value"><%= number_with_delimiter(@census["total"]) %></span><span class="label">prompts</span></div>
      <div class="job-stat"><span class="value"><%= number_with_delimiter(@census["mapped"]) %></span><span class="label">mapped</span></div>
      <div class="job-stat"><span class="value"><%= @census["topics"] %></span><span class="label">topics</span></div>
      <div class="job-stat"><span class="value"><%= @census["roots"] %></span><span class="label">phrase roots</span></div>
      <div class="job-stat"><span class="value"><%= @census["parts"] %></span><span class="label">parts</span></div>
      <div class="job-stat"><span class="value"><%= @labels["fields"].size %></span><span class="label">meme labels</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <%= link_to "library JSON", library_datasets_path(limit: 25), class: "btn btn-secondary btn-sm" %>
      <%= link_to "draw one", draw_datasets_path, class: "btn btn-secondary btn-sm" %>
      <%= link_to "meme labels JSON", meme_labels_datasets_path, class: "btn btn-secondary btn-sm" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<%# THE CARDS LIVE IN A PARTIAL: the same markup is what the FLUX page's
    DATASETS popup fetches, so the library has one definition rather than a
    page and a popup that drift. See datasets/_surface.html.erb. %>
<%= render "datasets/surface" %>